{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2509","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2509","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2509\",\"parent_revision\":\"a8681db62314e86bb5bd300fdf2c9cdd8c2cc7e9d15cb299bce53dc013131e14\",\"root_revision\":\"a8681db62314e86bb5bd300fdf2c9cdd8c2cc7e9d15cb299bce53dc013131e14\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`sam_plan(action='create')` writes plan YAML to `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/plan/*.yaml` on local disk and registers only a path pointer via `artifact_register` \u2014 without `content=`. Plans are therefore invisible to CI environments, worktree-isolated agents, and fresh checkouts. The policy (documented in CLAUDE.md prohibited patterns) requires all artifacts to be stored via `artifact_register(content=...)` so they live in GitHub/Gist and are retrievable from any environment via `artifact_read`.\\n\\nObserved during planning session for issue #2498 (plan P3e7e163d). After `sam_plan create` ran and the task-plan artifact was auto-registered, `backlog_view` showed `plan_path: null` \u2014 the content was not reachable via `artifact_read`, only via the local filesystem path.\\n\\nImpact: Every SAM plan is machine-local. Plans do not survive a fresh checkout, cannot be read by CI, cannot be accessed by worktree-isolated agents, and are silently absent in any environment other than the one where they were created.\\n\\n**User-provided context**: The fix direction is to have `sam_plan create` serialize the plan YAML and call `artifact_register(item_id=issue, artifact_type=\\\"task-plan\\\", content=yaml_string)` so the plan content is uploaded to GitHub Gist and retrievable via `artifact_read` from any environment. `sam_plan read/update` would then route through `artifact_read` \u2192 mutate \u2192 `artifact_register` rather than local file I/O.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**verdict**: VERIFIED\\n**claim**: sam_plan create writes plan YAML to local disk\\n**evidence**: sam_schema/server.py:320 calls _try_register_task_plan_artifact after LocalYamlTaskBackend creates the file; the plan path is a local ~/.dh/ path\\n**source**: sam_schema/server.py:180-232 (read 2026-05-30)\\n\\n---\\n\\n**verdict**: VERIFIED\\n**claim**: Content upload to Gist exists but silently swallows failures\\n**evidence**: sam_schema/server.py:211-224 \u2014 inner try/except catches BacklogError, OSError and only calls _log.warning(), returning without signalling failure to the caller\\n**source**: sam_schema/server.py:211-224 (read 2026-05-30)\\n\\n---\\n\\n**verdict**: VERIFIED\\n**claim**: sam_plan read/update/claim/state use LocalYamlTaskBackend, not artifact_read\\n**evidence**: sam_schema/server.py dispatches to backend.read_task(), backend.update_task(), etc. \u2014 LocalYamlTaskBackend reads/writes ~/.dh/ YAML files exclusively\\n**source**: sam_schema/server.py:257, 611, 649 (read 2026-05-30)\\n\\n---\\n\\n**verdict**: VERIFIED\\n**claim**: artifact_read MCP tool already does Gist-first retrieval with local fallback\\n**evidence**: backlog_core/server.py:2910-2930 \u2014 explicitly calls read_artifact_content_from_remote() first, then falls back to read_artifact_content() (local filesystem)\\n**source**: backlog_core/server.py:2866-2930 (read 2026-05-30)\\n\\n---\\n\\n**verdict**: VERIFIED\\n**claim**: The GitHub task backend (#984) exists but is incomplete\\n**evidence**: CLAUDE.md documents: 'github not yet fully implemented (#984) and raises NotImplementedError'\\n**source**: plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md backend section (read 2026-05-30)\\n\\n<!-- artifact-gist:eab83c56934af5308d485f87aff3f5dc -->\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Snapshot: sam_plan stores task plans as local YAML files violating plan-to-MCP policy\\nDate: 2026-05-30\\nGoal: All sam_plan operations (create, read, update, claim, state, list) must route through MCP artifact storage (artifact_register/artifact_read) so plans are retrievable from any environment without a local filesystem.\\nConditions:\\n1. Current plan storage location | Status: AVAILABLE \u2014 ~/.dh/projects/{slug}/plan/*.yaml (LocalYamlTaskBackend)\\n2. sam_plan create already uploads content to Gist via _try_register_task_plan_artifact | Status: AVAILABLE \u2014 code confirmed at sam_schema/server.py:211-224, but in a nested try/except that swallows upload failures silently\\n3. sam_plan read/update/claim/state use LocalYamlTaskBackend \u2014 never artifact_read | Status: AVAILABLE \u2014 confirmed: sam_schema/core/backends/local_yaml.py is sole backend for all read/write operations\\n4. artifact_read MCP tool already supports remote-first retrieval (Gist \u2192 local fallback) | Status: AVAILABLE \u2014 backlog_core/server.py:2910-2930 confirmed\\n5. GitHubTaskProvider exists but is incomplete (#984) | Status: DERIVABLE \u2014 check sam_schema/core/backends/ for github_task.py and NotImplementedError coverage\\n6. Whether Gist content upload actually succeeds in practice | Status: DERIVABLE \u2014 check _try_register_task_plan_artifact logs or reproduce with a real plan creation\\n7. Concurrency safety for plan updates (multiple agents updating task status simultaneously) | Status: DERIVABLE \u2014 LocalYamlTaskBackend uses file I/O; replacing with Gist read-modify-write has different concurrency properties\\n8. Test coverage for sam_schema backends | Status: DERIVABLE \u2014 check tests_sam/ for LocalYaml vs GitHub backend coverage\\n9. Backward compatibility: existing plans in ~/.dh/ | Status: DERIVABLE \u2014 need migration strategy or dual-read (local then remote) for existing plans\\nAVAILABLE count: 4\\nDERIVABLE count: 5\\nMISSING count: 0\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **sam_plan stores task plans as local yaml files violating plan-to-mcp policy** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 plan P3e7e163d for issue #2498, 2026-05-30\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-05-30\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-05-30)\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\nReproducible by reading a plan from any environment other than the one where it was created:\\n\\n```bash\\n# On machine A: create a plan\\nsam_plan create issue=42 ...  # writes ~/.dh/projects/.../plan/P{id}.yaml\\n\\n# On machine B or fresh checkout:\\nsam_plan read plan=P{id}  # fails: file not found at ~/.dh/...\\n```\\n\\nAlso reproducible within a single session for worktree-isolated agents: the agent runs in a separate worktree where ~/.dh/ is the same path, but if the original worktree was cleaned up or ran on a different host, sam_plan read fails.\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n**P1** \u2014 Affects every SAM-planned feature across all sessions. The workaround (running all sam_plan operations from the same machine) is fragile and breaks CI integration. User has been tracking this for months.\\n\\nEffort: medium-high (requires replacing LocalYamlTaskBackend read/write path with artifact_read/artifact_register; ~3-5 focused tasks)\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nAfter fix:\\n1. `sam_plan(action='create', issue=N)` stores the full plan YAML via `artifact_register(content=yaml_string)` in GitHub/Gist\\n2. `sam_plan(action='read', plan=P{id})` retrieves via `artifact_read` \u2014 works from any machine or CI environment\\n3. `sam_plan(action='update')` / claim / state operations perform read-modify-write through the artifact layer\\n4. Local disk may be used as a cache, but never as the sole source of truth\\n5. Existing plans in ~/.dh/ can still be read (migration path or dual-read: check Gist first, fall back to local)\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- [ ] `sam_plan(action='create', issue=N)` calls `artifact_register(content=yaml_string)` and the content is retrievable via `artifact_read(item_id=N, artifact_type='task-plan')` from a fresh session with no ~/.dh/ state\\n- [ ] `sam_plan(action='read', plan=P{id})` returns plan data when the local ~/.dh/ path does not exist (Gist-first retrieval)\\n- [ ] All sam_plan mutation operations (claim, state, update, append_task) persist changes to GitHub/Gist so a subsequent read from any machine sees the updated state\\n- [ ] Existing local plans at ~/.dh/ are still readable (backward compatibility / migration path)\\n- [ ] `uv run pytest tests_sam/ -q` passes with the new backend\\n- [ ] `fastmcp list --command 'uv run --script scripts/run_sam_server.py'` returns same tool count\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n**Core changes:**\\n- `sam_schema/server.py` \u2014 _try_register_task_plan_artifact: make content= upload non-best-effort; sam_plan read/update to route through artifact layer\\n- `sam_schema/core/backends/local_yaml.py` \u2014 add Gist-backed read path OR replace with artifact-native backend\\n- `sam_schema/core/backends/github_task.py` \u2014 complete the partial GitHub task backend (or build simpler artifact-native backend)\\n\\n**Documentation:**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` \u2014 update task.backend gotcha after fix\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/backend-providers.md` \u2014 update GitHub backend status\\n\\n**Tests:**\\n- `tests_sam/` \u2014 add cross-environment read tests (no local file, Gist content only)\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n**Blocking this item:**\\n- None \u2014 the artifact provider (Gist storage) and artifact_read MCP tool are already working\\n\\n**Related:**\\n- Issue #984 \u2014 incomplete GitHub TaskBackend (same problem space; this item may supersede or incorporate #984)\\n- Issue #2510 \u2014 add-new-feature delegates backlog_update(plan=) to subagent (separate bug, independent fix)\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\n**Estimate**: medium-high\\n- Understand artifact-native read/write path: 1 hour\\n- Implement Gist-backed plan read in sam_plan (create non-breaking dual-read): 2-3 hours\\n- Make all sam_plan mutations write-through to Gist: 2-3 hours\\n- Migration/backward-compat for existing ~/.dh/ plans: 1-2 hours\\n- Tests: 1-2 hours\\n- Total: 7-11 hours\\n\\nEffort: medium-high\\n\\n### Agent Instructions (instruct AI to use current interface)\\n\\n- None \u2014 agent skills use sam_plan MCP tools; interface unchanged\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Consumers (read the changed interface)\\n\\n- `backlog_core/server.py` \u2014 artifact_read MCP tool already supports Gist-first retrieval (no change needed)\\n- Every skill/agent that calls `sam_plan(action='read')` \u2014 benefits from fix, no interface change\\n- `dh:implement-feature` skill \u2014 dispatches tasks via sam_plan; cross-machine reads become possible\\n- CI environments that try to read plan state \u2014 currently fail (local file missing); fixed by this change\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Other References\\n\\n- `sam_schema/core/backends/` \u2014 existing backends: local_yaml.py, memory.py, beads.py, github_task.py (partial)\\n- `sam_schema/core/task_backend.py` \u2014 TaskBackend Protocol definition\\n- `dh_paths.py` \u2014 plan_dir() resolution; may need to stay for cache path even after MCP-native storage\\n- `.dh/config.yaml` \u2014 task.backend selection; default will change from 'local' to 'github' once implemented\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Producers (write the changed interface)\\n\\n- `sam_schema/server.py` \u2014 sam_plan MCP tool, _try_register_task_plan_artifact: must make content upload non-optional and propagate failures\\n- `sam_schema/core/backends/local_yaml.py` \u2014 LocalYamlTaskBackend: must be replaced or wrapped with MCP-native read/write\\n\\n### Concerns\\n\\n- [x] artifact_registry_client.py lines 156 and 246: `except (BacklogError, OSError, Exception)` \u2014 broad catch, BLE001/redundant, from T1 code outside T5 scope (reported by python-pytest-architect on T5) \u2192 tracked as cs-mz9\\n\\n### Configuration / CI\\n\\n- `.dh/config.yaml` \u2014 task.backend config; default should switch after fix is validated\\n\\n### Documentation (will become stale)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` \u2014 'task.backend: local' gotcha warning; update after fix\\n- `docs/backend-providers.md` \u2014 SAM task backend section; update GitHub backend status\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n\\n- [ ] sam_plan create stores content via artifact_register(content=) not local file\\n- [ ] sam_plan read retrieves via artifact_read (Gist-first, local cache fallback)\\n- [ ] sam_plan update does read-modify-write through artifact layer\\n- [ ] Existing local plans can still be read (migration or dual-read strategy)\\n- [ ] CLAUDE.md task.backend gotcha warning updated\\n- [ ] docs/backend-providers.md updated\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\n\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\n**Type**: defect\\n**Rationale**: The behavior (plans stored only on local disk) contradicts the documented policy (artifact_register with content= is mandatory per CLAUDE.md). This is a traceable failure: sam_plan create calls _try_register_task_plan_artifact which has a working content upload path, but the overall system design keeps LocalYamlTaskBackend as the sole read/write path, so the Gist upload is a disconnected side-channel that doesn't fix the portability problem.\\n**Analysis Method**: Source code trace \u2014 confirmed the three callsites that bypass artifact_read for plan operations\\n**Scenario Target**: Multi-environment SAM execution (CI, worktrees, fresh checkouts) \u2192 zero plan-not-found failures\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n\\n- **sam_schema/server.py** \u2014 FastMCP SAM server, all sam_plan operations\\n- **sam_schema/core/backends/local_yaml.py** \u2014 current plan storage (5+ methods to replace)\\n- **sam_schema/core/backends/github_task.py** \u2014 existing partial GitHub backend (incomplete)\\n- **backlog_core/artifact_provider.py** \u2014 GitHubGistArtifactProvider (already working)\\n- **backlog_core/server.py:2866** \u2014 artifact_read (already supports Gist-first)\\n\",\"digest\":\"9c13ed3fcd73c1aa79cb276352a0e61afb472f6178e51c82028b2661036b2ebb\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCN95Q\"}"}